## Testing with Thunder Client

Open Thunder Client in VS Code (⚡ icon in the sidebar) and run the following tests **in order**:

### Test 1 — Register a User

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Method | `POST` |
| URL | `http://localhost:3000/auth/register` |
| Body (JSON) | `{"name": "Alice", "email": "student@test.com", "password": "123456"}` |

**Expected:** `201 Created`



> ![register](<Screenshot 2026-05-17 114440.png>)

---

### Test 2 — Login

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Method | `POST` |
| URL | `http://localhost:3000/auth/login` |
| Body (JSON) | `{"email": "student@test.com", "password": "123456"}` |

**Expected:** `200 OK` with a token in the response

>  **Copy the token** — you will need it for Test 3.


> (![Test 2 - Login](<Screenshot 2026-05-17 112419.png>))


---

### Test 3 — Access Protected Route (Valid Token)

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Method | `GET` |
| URL | `http://localhost:3000/profile` |
| Header | `Authorization: Bearer <your token>` |

**Expected:** `200 OK` with user data

> ![vaild token](<Screenshot 2026-05-17 113608.png>)


---

### Test 4 — No Token (Should Fail)

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Method | `GET` |
| URL | `http://localhost:3000/profile` |
| Header | *(none)* |

**Expected:** `401 Unauthorized`

>![No token](<Screenshot 2026-05-17 113700.png>)


---

### Test 5 — Fake Token (Should Fail)

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Method | `GET` |
| URL | `http://localhost:3000/profile` |
| Header | `Authorization: Bearer thisisafaketoken` |

**Expected:** `403 Forbidden`

> ![Fake token](<Screenshot 2026-05-17 113805.png>)

---

### Test 6 — Register Second User

Same as Test 1 but with Bob's details:

```json
